  data: {
    LLM: 'First player leads any tile and declares which end is open. Play is clockwise or counter-clockwise (alternates by deal). Each turn: play a matching tile and call the new open end, or discard one tile face down and call drink. If three players drink in succession, the last player who played plays again. If no one can match, the game is blocked and ends; count unplayed tiles as well.',
    Player: 'First player leads any tile and declares which end is open. Play is clockwise or counter-clockwise (alternates by deal). Each turn: play a matching tile and call the new open end, or discard one tile face down and call drink. If three players drink in succession, the last player who played plays again. If no one can match, the game is blocked and ends; count unplayed tiles as well.',
    objective: 'On your turn, play a tile that matches the single open end of the layout and call the new open end, or if unable, discard one tile face down and say drink. The player with fewest pips on discarded and unplayed tiles wins the deal and leads the next. Pairs settle by pip difference.',
    gameplay: 'First player leads any tile and declares which end is open. Play is clockwise or counter-clockwise (alternates by deal). Each turn: play a matching tile and call the new open end, or discard one tile face down and call drink. If three players drink in succession, the last player who played plays again. If no one can match, the game is blocked and ends; count unplayed tiles as well.',
